It has been already pointed out that omp_get_num_threads() returns 1 in sequential sections of the code. Accordingly, even if setting, by omp_set_num_threads() , an overall number of threads larger than 1 , any call to omp_get_num_threads() will return 1 , unless we are in a parallel section. The example below tries to clarify this point #include <stdio.h>

