I have edited my question after previous comments (especially @Zboson) for better readability I have always acted on, and observed, the conventional wisdom that the number of openmp threads should roughly match the number of hyper-threads on a machine for optimal performance. However, I am observing odd behaviour on my new laptop with Intel Core i7 4960HQ, 4 cores - 8 threads. (See Intel docs here ) Here is my test code: #include <math.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <omp.h>

int main() {
    const int n = 256*8192*100;
    double *A, *B;
    posix_memalign((void**)&A, 64, n*sizeof(double));
    posix_memalign((void**)&B, 64, n*sizeof(double));
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
