I'm currently implementing an dynamic programming algorithm for solving knapsack problems. Therefore my code has two for-loops, an outer and an inner loop. From the logical point of view I can parallelize the inner for loop since the calculations there are independant from each other. The outer for loop can not be parallelized because of dependancies. So this was my first approach : for(int i=1; i < itemRows; i++){
