point2d myPoint; But there is a work around which will work with MSVC (as well as GCC and ICC).  You can use threadprivate pointers. The purpuse of threadprivate is to have private version of an object/type for each thread and have the values persistent between parallel regions. You can do that by delcaring a pointer to point2d , making that threadprivate, and then allocating memory for the private pointer for each thread in a parallel region. Make sure you delete the allocated memory at your last parallel call. #include <stdio.h>
